    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0542" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2635a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-05T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2976. Please telegraph me what use, if any, you have made of Department’s
                    circular April 27 regarding attitude of this Government <pb facs="0543" n="257"
                        xml:id="pg257"/> on the subject of armed merchant ships,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d336-f1"/> and whether it was made known to the German Government
                    before the dispatch of its note on submarine warfare which you are now
                    sending.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d336-f1" n="1" xml:id="d336-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. This is a summary of the Department’s memorandum published on the
                    same date. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg244">p.
                        244</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
